apparent that they just use

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:34.533 align:start position:0%
that as a sort of defense
mechanism, try and shut you up.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:36.669 align:start size:88% position:13%
But I think that really,
that time has passed.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.870
I think everyone's -

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.172
- 10 Years later, the
words don't matter

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:41.773 align:start size:81% position:19%
as much as they
used to back then.

00:05:41.773 --> 00:05:43.742 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Exactly, everyone's
like immune

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:45.777 align:start size:84% position:16%
to that kind of
attack now, and, yeah.

00:05:45.777 --> 00:05:47.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I just started
talking about these things

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:50.716 align:start size:84% position:16%
from my perspective,
which really is

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:52.751
still the perspective of a
classical liberal, you know.

00:05:52.751 --> 00:05:57.456 align:start size:97% position:3%
I've developed an
appreciation of conservatism,

00:05:57.456 --> 00:06:00.326
like real sort of halfy
conservatism, you know,

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:03.929
the sort of genuine of bonds
of sentiment that tie together

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:97% position:3%
people and place and community
building outwards to nation

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to humanity, you know,
I've really spent a lot

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:12.104
of time reading their philosophy

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:13.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
because they're actually
really bad at articulating it.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.207 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, you probably
can't actually name

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:17.176 align:start size:84% position:16%
