be treated as individuals

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.299
in decent ways,

00:06:41.299 --> 00:06:43.569 align:start size:97% position:3%
but there's more to the
good life than just being an

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:46.005 align:start size:84% position:16%
atomized individual
on your own, you know,

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:48.640
with just a bunch of things
given to you by the state.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.310
There's actually a lot more
to the good life than that.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.846
And so, yeah, I just
continued developing.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:58.117
I've matured a lot, which
is never fun to say, right?

00:06:58.117 --> 00:06:59.318
(Dave laughing)

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:00.520 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because it's, you know,
you realize, well -

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.754 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It depends where
you end up, I suppose.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.255
- Well, yeah, yeah, but
it's never fun to say.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:05.858
But I've definitely matured a
lot and I started a business

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.293
